le but i like what they did  there and they didn't panic they didn't  go crazy and that's really what the  ravens mo is they are an organization  that has a mission they don't panic they  don't go you know nuts in free agency  they don't try to get the splashiest guy  i think they always build the team the  right way and i've always been impressed  with it it all comes down to lamar  jackson though with all that said this  is the off season can't be graded until  we find out what lamar jackson has done  to progress as a passer in the nfl  that's it because you can assign all you  want you can bring everyone all you want  in there but if lamar jackson can't at  least keep defenses honest because  there's now the books out on them you  saw the chargers game he was phenomenal  in la in that first matchup then they  play them this in the playoffs second  look the first team to get a second look  and the chargers win that game so lamar  jackson's growth is everything  especially considering the fact that  he's obviously on the rookie year rookie  contract and you can build around  something like that that's kind of the  the blueprint so to speak for the nfl so  wherever lamar jackson goes that's where  the baltimore ravens go yeah take full  advantage of the next few years spend  the money elsewhere before you have to  pay lamar jackson and defensively you  know they just kind of shrug the way the  steelers of the 90s did when star  players walk away in free agency they  won't overpay to keep them see you later  cj mosley they lost ultimately four key  players on defense terrell suggs a guy  we never thought would play for another  team he moves on eric weddle moves on  zadaria smith signs with the packers but  then they go out and they spend big  money on earl thomas i mean this is a  guy who's broken the same leg twice  there were concerns about what he would  be worth on the open market they came  out of nowhere they shocked everyone  with the deal they gave to earl t